  body: "# Carer’s Allowance caring condition\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source defines a caring week
    beginning on Sunday and describes regular care of at least 35 hours in that week, allowing care on fewer than
    seven days and considering an intention to care.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is one CA condition, not
    a complete entitlement test. The source’s dated rule from 17 August 1993 does not aggregate care hours for different
    severely disabled people. Earnings, education, residence, qualifying disability payment, breaks and Memos 12/23
    and 12-25 remain separate dependencies.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 60035, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 60036, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 60037, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 60044, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=7).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch60`:
    PDF `ab9fed933c167b4ac18039204c3853c425731ffb4239022a11b41884caaee22a`; extracted pages `bc5925c0d434fbc4bec575bea2e1e2dbd020b014497ab156973054e80e326f2f`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.596227Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=5
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/ca-qualifying-disability-payment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The caring condition refers to a specifically defined severely disabled person; that definition
      is linked to qualifying payments.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0005
      quote: "60035 For the caring condition to be satisfied in any week, claimants must show that in that week
        they\n\n\n1. are or\n\n\n2. are likely to be\n\n\nengaged and regularly engaged in caring for a severely
        disabled person for at least 35 hours a week 1 (see\n\nDMG 60045). For CA, a “caring week” means a period
        of seven days beginning on a Sunday 2.\n\n\n                                                           \
        \    1 SS (ICA) Regs, reg 4(1); 2 SS CB Act 92, s 122(1)"
      locator: DMG 60035
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0004
      quote: "60033 [see DMG memo 02/25] “Severely disabled person” means a person for whom\n\n\n1. AA1 or\n\n\n\
        2. the care component of DLA at the highest or middle rate or pension age disability\npayment2 or\n\n3.
        CAA payable as\n\n\n       3.1 an increase of IIDB3 or\n\n\n       3.2 an increase of an old scheme allowance4
        or\n\n\n       3.3 an increase of WC5 or\n\n\n       3.4 a WDisP6 or\n\n\n4. the daily living component
        of PIP at the standard or enhanced rate 7 or"
      locator: DMG 60033
  - target: term/ca-care-statement-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source specifies how to treat the claimant’s statement about care hours.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0006
      quote: "60040 The claimant’s statement that the required number of hours are spent in caring should be\naccepted
        without further enquiry unless there is good reason to doubt it.\n\n\nExample\n\n\nDenise and Lesley both
        claim CA for caring for Mick who is a severely disabled person. The DM decides\nto make further enquiries
        to establish who is entitled to CA (see DMG 60026)."
      locator: DMG 60040
  - target: term/ca-temporary-care-break
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source contains a separate mechanism for temporary breaks from the caring condition.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0007
      quote: "60045 A week when a person does not satisfy the “caring condition” is treated as a week in which that\n\
        condition is satisfied, if that person\n\n\n1. has only temporarily ceased to satisfy the “caring condition”
        and\n\n\n2. has satisfied the caring condition for at least 14 weeks in a 26 week period. The 26 week period
        ends\nwith the first week that person no longer satisfied the caring condition and\n\n\n3. would have satisfied
        it for at least 22 weeks in the 26 week period described in DMG 60045 2., but for\nthe fact that\n\n\n \
        \     3.1 either that person or\n\n\n      3.2 the severely disabled person\n\n\nwas undergoing medical
        or other treatment, as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution 1.\n\n\n                     \
        \                                                                1 SS (ICA) Regs, reg 4(2)"
      locator: DMG 60045
